# Shell scripts MUST keep LF endings so the bash shebang and `set -euo pipefail`
# work when the repo is checked out on Windows (autocrlf would otherwise inject
# CRLF and break scripts/ci_no_permissive_rls.sh in CI).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Recorded LLM responses are EVIDENCE, not source. They must be byte-identical
# to what the provider actually returned, on every platform — `core.autocrlf` is
# `true` in this repo, so without this rule the same fixture is CRLF in a Windows
# working tree and LF in a Cloud Build container. A regression fixture that
# differs between where it is authored and where it is asserted is not a fixture.
# Phase 15.4 turns on the exact bytes of these files: the two coffee responses
# use the literal string `<TAB>`, the other two use U+0009, and telling those
# apart is the whole point.
tribunal/nestor_pulse_sdk/tests/fixtures/**/responses/*.txt text eol=lf
